  "name": "TYPHIFAST",
  "code": "2860",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>-This test is for qualitative detection and differentiation of IgG and IgM anti-Salmonella typhi &amp; paratyphi antibodies in human serum.<br>-All test results must always be correlated with clinical findings. The test is qualitative assay and is not for quantitative determination of antibody concentration levels.<br>-A negative result can occur if the quantity of anti-Salmonella typhi and paratyphi antibodies present in the specimen is below the detection limit of the assay, or the antibodies that are detected are not present during the stage of disease in which a sample is collected.<br>-The specimen containing unusually high titre of heterophile antibodies or rheumatoid factor may affect expected results.<br>-The results obtained with this test should be interpreted in conjunction with other diagnostic procedures and clinical findings.</p>",
